menu "Padel Remote"

config PADEL_REMOTE_WIFI_CHANNEL
    int "Wi-Fi channel"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    help
        ESP-NOW channel. Must match the court until channel handover via
        PAIR_ASSIGN is exercised on hardware.

config PADEL_REMOTE_BUTTON_GPIO
    int "Point button GPIO"
    default 3
    help
        Active-low button input with internal pull-up. Default GPIO3 = pad
        D1 on the XIAO ESP32-C3. Verify against docs/HARDWARE_PINOUT.md on
        bring-up day.

config PADEL_REMOTE_PRESS_MS
    int "Press debounce / minimum press (ms)"
    range 30 600
    default 150
    help
        How long the button must stay down before the press counts. The
        default 150 ms rejects the accidental brushes players produce with a
        shirt or a racket while still feeling instant on a deliberate press.
        Raise it if a court still records phantom points; the undo hold
        (1500 ms) puts the ceiling on how far this can go.

config PADEL_REMOTE_LED_GPIO
    int "Feedback LED GPIO"
    default 10
    help
        External feedback LED (the XIAO ESP32-C3 has no user LED on board).
        Default GPIO10 = pad D10. Active high.

config PADEL_REMOTE_SLEEP_ENABLE
    bool "Deep sleep after inactivity"
    default y
    help
        Deep sleep once remote_core reports nothing outstanding for
        PADEL_REMOTE_SLEEP_TIMEOUT_S, waking on the point button (spec 11.4
        step 3). Requires the button to sit on GPIO0-5, the only pins that
        can wake an ESP32-C3 from deep sleep. Turn this off for bench work:
        a sleeping remote drops off the serial monitor.

config PADEL_REMOTE_SLEEP_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Inactivity timeout before deep sleep (seconds)"
    depends on PADEL_REMOTE_SLEEP_ENABLE
    range 5 86400
    default 900
    help
        Idle time before the remote sleeps. The default 15 minutes is far
        longer than any gap between points, so it only triggers between
        sessions. Shorten it to exercise sleep/wake cycles on the bench.

endmenu
